      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C61", "C78", "C110", "C76", "C82", "C87", "C89"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability or IV-comparison measurement for the query molecule itself.",
    "No L3 record for the query or its exact fentiapril-like thiol-ACE-inhibitor scaffold; closest records are enalapril/perindopril/ramipril prodrug-metabolite exposures.",
    "First-pass thiol metabolism (e.g., S-methylation, disulfide formation) and possible efflux are not directly assessed.",
    "The normal-condition perindoprilat value (19 ± 7%) is near threshold and from a prodrug-metabolite context, limiting its transferability."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F ≥ 20%) because the closest small-acid and phenylthio-containing analogs have measured oral bioavailability above 20% (pidotimod 42–44%, fenbendazole 27%, PBA 78%, ampicillin 29%, maraviroc 24–33%), and no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F < 20%; L3 oral AUC/Cmax records are prodrug/metabolite exposures that do not change the decision."
}

